BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:skyros-skyros-chora-feast-of-agios-georgios-patron-agios-georgios-m-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270422
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270424
SUMMARY:Feast of Agios Georgios (patron)\, Agios Georgios Monastery\, Chora
LOCATION:Skyros Chora\, Skyros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:St George is the patron of Skyros (the Venetians called it Isola San Giorgio) and his 10th-century monastery sits on the rock under the castle above the Chora. The feast on 23 April\, moved to Easter Monday when it falls in Lent\, is a liturgy and procession rather than a tavla panigiri\, but it is the day the Chora dresses up. Steep climb\; go up early and have coffee in the square afterwards.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skyros/#skyros-chora-feast-of-agios-georgios-patron-agios-georgios-m
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skyros/#skyros-chora-feast-of-agios-georgios-patron-agios-georgios-m
END:VEVENT
